 ### Seam Generation for Adjacent Chunks
-Generates mesh vertices and indices along the boundary between two adjacent octree chunks to eliminate seams common in dual contouring implementations [S5]. It initializes a `borderChildren` array of 8 pointers to `nullptr`, and an `idxs` array mapping chunk 0 to n1 and chunk 1 to n2. It iterates over both chunks, retrieves children arrays, and loops 4 times to fetch coordinates and edge indices from `edgeIndexLookup[dir][j][i]`. It computes octree indices, retrieves children, stores them in `borderChildren`, and generates vertex indices. Finally, it dispatches to the appropriate `FaceProc` function based on direction, passing the two octrees in the correct order to handle winding/normal consistency [S5]. The `edgeIndexLookup` is a 4D array of ints with shape `[6][2][4][4]`, where dimensions correspond to directions (x+, x-, y+, y-, z+, z-), chunk index (old/new), border points, and `{x, y, z, edgeIdx}` respectively [S5].
