 ## Background
-The octree-based variant extends standard Dual Contouring by using a hierarchical grid structure to represent the scalar field, allowing for adaptive resolution [S3, unofficial]. The method is based on works of Schaefer et al. (Manifold dual contouring) [S3, unofficial]. It is used in real destructible-voxel implementations (e.g., GPU dual contouring in Unity) which use classic octree LOD without meshlets [S1, unofficial].
